{"title":"1984 BMO Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_BMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/f/87f023210db680ae1d6d1c70b44339b20f96f94d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{1}, a_{2}, \\cdots, a_{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"106\" height=\"13\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/2/72287b09043ed45b372a517d764e12d07aff8071.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />) are positive real numbers with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/c/83c1a857f742ee6de89c06a25d637cda9df0fa10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{1} + a_{2} + \\cdots + a_{n} = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"176\" height=\"17\" />, prove that\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/a/25a18ee028bedddd742d1565ffcf92c55c0aedc2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a_{1}}{1 + a_{2} + a_{3} + \\cdots + a_{n}} + \\cdots + \\frac{a_{n}}{1 + a_{1} + a_{2} + \\cdots + a_{n - 1}} \\geq \\frac{n}{2n - 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"516\" height=\"38\" /></center>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_BMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can recognise that the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />th term of the left-hand side would be equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/8/228c9c02aef099c110aa645857f9f71b3c8bbafd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a_{k}}{2 - a_{k}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"55\" height=\"37\" /> because the sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/3/ec3db5902ad68d228c274abe25a4f6f3f8e5a3ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{1} + a_{2} + a_{3} + \\cdots + a_{n - 1} + a_{n} = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"273\" height=\"18\" />, so:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/d/74d0de4bc8160dd9060b02b02feed23df840b943.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a_{1}}{1 + a_{2} + a_{3} + \\cdots + a_{n}} + \\cdots + \\frac{a_{n}}{1 + a_{1} + a_{2} + \\cdots + a_{n - 1}} = \\frac{a_{1}}{2 - a_{1}} + \\frac{a_{2}}{2 - a_{2}} + \\cdots + \\frac{a_{n - 1}}{2 - a_{n - 1}} + \\frac{a_{n}}{2 - a_{n}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"800\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>To make this easier, we can create a function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37c84e206962bfb57e7ca635d86c7c309587229.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = \\frac{x}{2 - x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"107\" height=\"36\" />. This sum is then:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/7/0a744311b259665f0e7c5c19bf75304fdbc1f07a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a_{1}) + f(a_{2}) + f(a_{3}) + \\cdots + f(a_{n - 1}) + f(a_{n})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"365\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>We also realise that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/f/c4f8473eac20565df46e727e7b9f14fca92a9ec9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"13\" /> is on the interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/5/6457ca2dcd40dc21d9aa0db18c66bbac9af4d899.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/2/72287b09043ed45b372a517d764e12d07aff8071.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> and each are positive real numbers that sum up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> (which would only be possible if each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/f/c4f8473eac20565df46e727e7b9f14fca92a9ec9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"13\" /> is on the interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/5/6457ca2dcd40dc21d9aa0db18c66bbac9af4d899.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />). We can then check if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is convex by using its second derivative:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/b/c3b41381b593b735fa4ac008ab049cd9e3211d20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f&#39;(x) = \\frac{(2 - x) \\times \\frac{d}{dx}(x) - x \\times \\frac{d}{dx}(2 - x)}{(2 - x)^{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"320\" height=\"47\" />, which simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/2/cf23a079db2ddd6878959f759d468526c14d64b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = \\frac{2}{(2 - x)^{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"129\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/d/81dc2d4bb65970dd0bcd899ed42a7317be73ed62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f&#39;&#39;(x) = \\frac{(2 - x)^{2} \\times \\frac{d}{dx}(2) - 2 \\times \\frac{d}{dx}([2 - x]^{2})}{[(2 - x)^{2}]^{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"346\" height=\"47\" />, which simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b2b19caf9cfd2cbc710e9a24b774b2d0b6b7048.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{(2 - x)^{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"69\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p><p>Since each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/f/c4f8473eac20565df46e727e7b9f14fca92a9ec9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"13\" /> is on the interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/5/6457ca2dcd40dc21d9aa0db18c66bbac9af4d899.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> we plug-in will also be on that interval. This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/1/64131e8aff8d1895be0b1874d69082a2014f5b8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 - x$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" /> will always be positive because it is positive if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/4/e84958f805b063032d2629160e880abc1487afa6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &lt; 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/a/3bae1afffe62b8b1b8b4c1024bcf7c7ba8bbed41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{(2 - x)^{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"69\" height=\"43\" /> will always be positive. Because the second derivative of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is always positive on the interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/5/6457ca2dcd40dc21d9aa0db18c66bbac9af4d899.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> will be strictly convex on the interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/5/6457ca2dcd40dc21d9aa0db18c66bbac9af4d899.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, applying <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Jensen%27s_inequality\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Jensen&#39;s inequality\">Jensen's inequality</a>, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/d/9cd160dbec751a5c87783405952361ee69d48c98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{f(a_{1}) + f(a_{2}) + f(a_{3}) + \\cdots + f(a_{n - 1}) + f(a_{n})}{n} \\geq f(\\frac{a_{1} + a_{2} + a_{3} + \\cdots + a_{n - 1} + a_{n}}{n})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"660\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/3/ec3db5902ad68d228c274abe25a4f6f3f8e5a3ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{1} + a_{2} + a_{3} + \\cdots + a_{n - 1} + a_{n} = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"273\" height=\"18\" />, the right-hand side simplifies to \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/c/d4c8a281740d27b596049cf66c3a6ecb6217618b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(\\frac{1}{n}) = \\frac{\\frac{1}{n}}{2 - \\frac{1}{n}} = \\frac{1}{2n - 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"193\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is a positive number, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/4/2343d131ea3a065245654e5989e7b35420948c7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a_{1}) + f(a_{2}) + f(a_{3}) + \\cdots + f(a_{n - 1}) + f(a_{n}) \\geq \\frac{n}{2n - 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"444\" height=\"36\" />\n</p><p>As established before, this was equal to the sum of everything on the left-hand side, so we then end up with\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/a/25a18ee028bedddd742d1565ffcf92c55c0aedc2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a_{1}}{1 + a_{2} + a_{3} + \\cdots + a_{n}} + \\cdots + \\frac{a_{n}}{1 + a_{1} + a_{2} + \\cdots + a_{n - 1}} \\geq \\frac{n}{2n - 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"516\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Cauchy-Schwarz.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Cauchy-Schwarz)\">Solution 2 (Cauchy-Schwarz)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_BMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Cauchy-Schwarz)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><i>This problem needs a solution. If you have a solution for it, please help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1984_BMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit\">adding it</a></span>.</i> \n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018141234\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.020 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.037 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 210/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 423/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8080/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.148      1 Template:Solution\n100.00%    7.148      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:38071:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018141234 and revision id 293834. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}